From: Seeed Rockchip BSP
Subject: [PATCH] pxe: expand environment macros in the FDTOVERLAYS directive

cmd/pxe.c runs the APPEND directive through cli_simple_process_macros()
in label_boot() (and again for the final bootargs), but uses the
FDTOVERLAYS list as it was parsed.  A board that wants the overlay list to
come from its boot environment - so that one extlinux.conf serves both the
"no overlays" and the "apply these overlays" case without rewriting a file
that lives on a read-only rootfs - therefore cannot express it as ${...}:
the literal text is handed to the loader as a file name and every boot
logs "Failed loading overlay ${fdtoverlays}".

Expand the directive the same way APPEND is expanded.  An undefined
variable expands to the empty string and the loader already skips empty
entries, so boards that never set the variable keep applying nothing.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/cmd/pxe.c	2026-09-21 13:47:30.890951998 +0800
+++ b/cmd/pxe.c	2026-09-21 13:47:30.890951998 +0800
@@ -610,13 +610,24 @@
 #ifdef CONFIG_OF_LIBFDT_OVERLAY
 static void label_boot_fdtoverlay(cmd_tbl_t *cmdtp, struct pxe_label *label)
 {
-	char *fdtoverlay = label->fdtoverlays;
+	char fdtoverlay_buf[CONFIG_SYS_CBSIZE];
+	char *fdtoverlay = fdtoverlay_buf;
 	struct fdt_header *working_fdt;
 	char *fdtoverlay_addr_env;
 	ulong fdtoverlay_addr;
 	ulong fdt_addr;
 	int err;
 
+	/*
+	 * Expand ${...} macros, exactly like label_boot() does for the APPEND
+	 * directive.  The overlay list can then come from the environment, so
+	 * an extlinux.conf carrying "FDTOVERLAYS ${fdtoverlays}" applies
+	 * whatever the variable holds and applies nothing when it is unset.
+	 * Without this the literal ${fdtoverlays} would be taken for a file
+	 * name and fail to load.
+	 */
+	cli_simple_process_macros(label->fdtoverlays, fdtoverlay_buf);
+
 	/* Get the main fdt and map it */
 	fdt_addr = simple_strtoul(env_get("fdt_addr_r"), NULL, 16);
 	working_fdt = map_sysmem(fdt_addr, 0);
